$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357686 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3dc7c55-f986-54b3-95d7-1e0702bd8e87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357686 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394874 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9e354856-dfba-5b4c-b973-04f47aaf9d4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218639